<title>FRANCE: ADP air cargo exports traffic up 8.4 pct in Nov.</title>
<headline>ADP air cargo exports traffic up 8.4 pct in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Export traffic from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 53,722 tonnes, in November or up 8.4 percent on a year ago, Aeroports de Paris, (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>ADP's global exports in November, by region, with percentage change on the same period 1995, was as follows:</p>
<p> Domestic		  3,888 tonnes  up    19.6pct</p>
<p> European Union	  6,785 tonnes  up    26.4</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	   1,420 tonnes  up    17.6</p>
<p> North Africa		852 tonnes  up     3.6</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa    4,523 tonnes  up     6.6</p>
<p> North America	  15,178 tonnes  up     7.1</p>
<p> French territories    2,088 tonnes  down  14.6</p>
<p> Latin America	   3,110 tonnes  up    24.6</p>
<p> Middle East	     4,915 tonnes  up     8.2</p>
<p> Far East		 10,963 tonnes  down   0.5</p>
<p> Total		    53,722 tonnes  up     8.4</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
